Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for a description of the "nvinferserver"
plugin and "nvdsinferserver" API.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- GStreamer-1.0 Development package
- GStreamer-1.0 Base Plugins Development package
- CUDA Runtime13.4.3 (CUDA_VER=13.4) for x86/SBSA, or13.2.2
  (CUDA_VER=13.2) for the JetPack7.2.2 Jetson upgrade target

Install gstreamer developement packages using:
   sudo apt-get install libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev libgstreamer1.0-dev

Other dependencies:
- Matching Triton26.10 C++ client SDK for x86/genericSBSA
- Separately qualified JetPack7.2.2/TRT11.4.1-compatible SDK for Jetson
- Google Protobuf compiler matching the selected Triton client SDK's headers
  and protobuf libraries

Install other dependencies (writing /opt requires root privileges):
1. Preprovision the complete matching client SDK at /opt/tritonclient, containing
include/grpc_client.h, include/common.h and the C++ libraries under lib/.
For x86/SBSA, the vendor26.10-py3-sdk container supplies /workspace/install;
select the matching architecture. No26.10 SDK ZIP URL is assumed or invented.
The build driver never pulls this image automatically. See build/BUILD.md and
https://github.com/triton-inference-server/server/releases/tag/v2.74.0.
For the dependency stage an alternate complete location may be supplied using
TRITON_CLIENT_SDK_ROOT; a standalone Makefile uses TRITON_GRPC_CLIENT instead.
Headers/library presence alone does not prove SDK release provenance.
For protobuf 6 and newer the inference core also requires the complete matching
static client/gRPC/protobuf/Abseil/upb archive set. Rebuild and install the core
before this plugin; copying a newer libgrpcclient.so onto an older core is not a
supported replacement. Configuration reflection and per-class filter lookups
must stay in the library owning those generated messages.

2. Supply the protoc compiler matching the selected SDK's protobuf headers and
libraries, and set PROTOBUF_BIN_DIR to its bin directory. Use the compiler from
that SDK's build or the corresponding official Protobuf release; do not assume
the system compiler or a hardcoded older v3.21.12 download is compatible. The
shared build rules verify the selected compiler version before regeneration.
The compiler executes on the build host; select its architecture accordingly.

Jetson requires its qualified matching SDK, not the genericSBSA image or a
legacy26.04 archive assumed compatible with TRT11.4.1. Apply the same matching
compiler/header/library requirement to that separately qualified provider.

Please ensure that the above dependencies are installed and update corresponding
paths in the Makefile if required.
Current set paths are as follows:
TRITON_GRPC_CLIENT ?= /opt/tritonclient
PROTOBUF_BIN_DIR ?= /opt/proto/bin

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:
Export or set in Makefile the appropriate CUDA_VER
Run make and sudo make install

NOTE:
1. To compile the sources, run make with "sudo" or root permission.
2. Update PATH variable with newly installed protoc by running below command,
   export PATH=/opt/proto/bin/:$PATH
3. Clean and build sources which are compiled with old protoc version.
